  "result": "I added reservations with expiry to the store and the API, and `npm test` passes (176 tests, 0 failed).\n\n- **Store (`src/store.js`):**\n  - `reserve`, `confirm`, `release` and `getAvailable` are new, and `removeItem` now checks against available stock.\n  - Time comes only from the store's `clock`.\n  - Expired reservations are ignored when computing availability and are not deleted from memory, so `confirm` on an expired id still returns `RESERVATION_EXPIRED`.\n- **API (`src/api.js`):** `GET /stock/:sku` now includes `available`, and the three reservation routes return the status codes you specified.\n- **Tests:** I added 7 store tests and 4 API tests. They cover expiry at exactly creation time + ttl, confirm errors, repeated release, and `removeItem` against reserved stock.\n\nTwo behaviors your spec didn't define:\n- `ttlMs` isn't validated.\n- Any error from `POST /reservations` other than `INSUFFICIENT_STOCK` returns 400 with the error message, and `POST /reservations/:id/confirm` returns 404 for any error other than `RESERVATION_EXPIRED`.",
